@page rh="FRONT MATTER · THE CANON THIS VOLUME RUNS ON" m="FINAL RULINGS; RULING; DECIDED"
# The canon this volume runs on
Every dossier was written against these. Where a file disagrees, the page prints the file's version as SUPERSEDED and moves on.
tabrl:
| Ruling | What it fixes |
| FR 0 | Solomon's father is the man Miriam was reassigned to after Thomas left. Zion is Thomas's. |
| FR 3 | Thomas left voluntarily in 2084, for another Dominion, another woman, another life. |
| FR 4–6 | Eden went to Celeste alone in 2085. The younger three came in 2090. Miriam left all four and went alone. |
| FR 11–16 | What each child saw on the day she left, what they were told, and the 2094 letter nobody received. Celeste has no proof Miriam is alive. |
| FR 17–18 | Miriam's father, his household, and why she came back |
| FR 19–25 | What the Trials do with all twelve women, and the rules around the Declaration |
| FR 26–34 | Hannah's career, Naomi, the 2085 cohort, and the Prelate's name |
| FR 35–44 | The House of Vane, the removed heir, and the documents |
| Ruling | Zion is eighteen. Solomon is sixteen. Leah is younger than Eden and sat for an assessment. Dorian is fifty-nine. Calla's surname is Merritt. |
small: Every ruling is printed in full in the back matter, with the conflicts it settles.

